{"rhinoceros":{"id":"3d47814c-be50-4688-a47d-10aa522caff7","word":"rhinoceros","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"herbivorous pachyderm with horn(s)","tags":["masculine"],"word":"rinoceronte"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Herein therefore to draw up our determinations beside the several pieces of Scripture mentioning this Animal (which some may well contend to be only meant of the Rhinoceros) we are so far from denying there is any Unicorn at all, that we affirme there are many kinds thereof. In the number of Quadrapedes we will concede no less then five; that is the Indian Oxe, Indian Ass, Rhinoceros, the Oryx, and that which is more eminently termed Monoceros, or Unicornis.","ref":"1658, Thomas Brown, “Of Unicorns Horn”, in Pseudodoxia Epidemica: Or Enquiries Into Very many Received Tenents And commonly Presumed Truths. The Fourth Edition, page 203:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[162,172],[376,386]],"id":"7dfacfdf-66ea-4946-892f-914f3bab17d3"}],"wikidata":["Q34718"],"senseid":["en:Q34718"],"links":[["herbivorous","herbivorous"],["ungulate","ungulate"],["mammal","mammal"],["Rhinocerotidae","Rhinocerotidae#Translingual"],["horn","horn"],["snout","snout"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Any large herbivorous ungulate mammal native to Africa and Asia of the family Rhinocerotidae, with thick, gray skin and one or two horns on their snouts."],"id":"833e0357-5dd6-4445-9f86-b8f2d3614752"},{"topics":["biology","history","human-sciences","natural-sciences","paleontology","sciences"],"categories":["en:Paleontology"],"links":[["paleontology","paleontology"],["Rhinocerotoidea","Rhinocerotoidea#Translingual"],["Paraceratherium","Paraceratherium#Translingual"]],"raw_glosses":["(paleontology) A member of the superfamily Rhinocerotoidea, including hornless members of the extinct genus Paraceratherium."],"glosses":["A member of the superfamily Rhinocerotoidea, including hornless mem