s with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Georgian translations","Terms with German Low German translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Kashubian translations","Terms with Latvian translations","Terms with Limburgish translations","Terms with Lithuanian translations","Terms with Low German translations","Terms with Lower Sorbian translations","Terms with Luxembourgish translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Mongolian translations","Terms with North Frisian translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translations","Terms with Occitan translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Rhine Franconian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Slovak translations","Terms with Slovene translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Upper Sorbian translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","Terms with West Flemish translations","Terms with West Frisian translations","Terms with Yiddish translations","en:Places in Germany","en:Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany","en:States of Germany"],"links":[["state","state"],["Germany","Germany#English"]],"glosses":["A state of modern Germany."],"id":"30aab8e2-371a-445d-ae36-138ceec4e693"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"rhizome":{"id":"d06828c5-7ebc-4fa7-b1da-efd84f803cf1","word":"rhizome","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"horizontal underground stem of some plants","tags":["masculine"],"word":"rizoma"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"All these species are climbing, briery plants, having long slender roots, which proceed in all directions from a common rootstalk or rhizome.","ref":"1868, George Bacon Wood, A Treatise on Therapeutics, and Pharmacology, Or Materia Medica, Philadelphia: J. B. Lippincott & Company, page 432:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[133,140]],"id":"d5496628-7371-44be-8486-1bb33980649f"}],"topics":["biology","botany","natural-sciences"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Botany"],"links":[["botany","botany"],["horizontal","horizontal"],["underground","underground"],["stem","stem"],["plant","plant"],["root","root"],["shoot","shoot"],["scion","scion"],["node","node"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"race"},{"word":"rootstalk"}],"raw_glosses":["(botany) A horizontal, underground stem of some plants that sends out roots and shoots (scions) from its nodes."],"glosses":["A horizontal, underground stem of some plants that sends out roots and shoots (scions) from its nodes."],"id":"2a928079-25a2-442a-b8f7-5f6a4c0437eb"},{"examples":[{"text":"The corpus of Kafka's writing, they argue, is ‘a rhizome, a burrow’ (K 7)—an uncentered and meandering growth like crab grass, a complex, aleatory network of pathways like a rabbit warren. A rhizome, as Deleuze and Guattari explain in Rhizome: an Introduction (1976), is the antithesis of a root-tree structure, or ‘arborescence’, the structural model which has dominated Western thought from Porphyrian trees, to Linnaean taxonomies, to Chomskyan sentence diagrams.","ref":"1989, Ronald Bogue, Deleuze and Guattari, Psychology Press, →ISBN, page 107:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[49,56],[191,198]],"id":"6608017f-3611-4de8-97d2-4b9edb2afb07"},{"text":"Critical theorists have often drawn from Deleuze and Guattari's notion of the rhizome when discussing the potential of the Internet. While the Internet may structurally appear as a rhizome, its day-to-day usage by millions via search engines precludes experiencing the random interconnectedness and potential democratizing function.","ref":"2008, A. Hess, “Reconsidering the Rhizome”, in Amanda Spink, Michael Zimmer, editors, Web Search: Multidisciplinary Perspectives, Springer Science & Business Media, →ISBN, page 35:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[78,85],[181,188]],"id":"7ceee63a-cdf8-4fbd-8119-29673b01dc6b"}],"topics":["human-sciences","philosophy","sciences"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Philosophy"],"links":[["philosophy","philosophy"],["apprehend","apprehend"],["multiplicities","multiplicity"]],"raw_glosses":["(philosophy, critical theory) A so-called “image of thought” that apprehends multiplicities."],"qualifier":"critical theory","glosses":["A so-called “image of thought” that apprehends multiplicities."],"id":"4acc671c-36fe-4408-91eb-ba4be38a8a3f"}],"related":[{"word":"licorice"},{"word":"mycorrhiza"}],"synonyms":[]},"Rhineland":{"id":"0461b2d0-deaf-43bf-a401-51bd073229f6","word":"Rhineland","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"land on both sides of the river Rhine","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Renânia"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["en:Geographic and cultural areas of Germany","en:Places in Germany"],"links":[["definite article","definite article#English"],["area","area"],["Rhine","Rhine#English"],["Germany","Germany#English"],["Prussian","Prussian"],["Rhineland-Palatinate","Rhineland-Palatinate"],["North Rhine-Westphalia","North Rhine-Westphalia"]],"raw_glosses":["(usually with the definite article) An area on both sides of the river Rhine, in the west of Germany. Roughly equivalent to the former Prussian Rhine Province, now the greater part of Rhineland-Palatinate plus the south-western half of North Rhine-Westphalia."],"glosses":["An area on both sides of the river Rhine, in the west of Germany. Roughly equivalent to the former Prussian Rhine Province, now the greater part of Rhineland-Palatinate plus the south-western half of North Rhine-Westphalia."],"tags":["usually"],"raw_tags":["with the definite article"],"id":"a6f658c2-3954-46ba-8151-4db091add0a7"},{"categories":["English terms with uncommon senses"],"raw_glosses":["(uncommon) All of Germany's territories on the Rhine."],"glosses":["All of Germany's territories on the Rhine."],"tags":["uncommon"],"id":"e873dba3-44a0-4bb5-b698-23f0b7a5d7bf"},{"categories":["en:Places in Missouri, USA","en:Places in the United States","en:Villages in Missouri, USA","en:Villages in the United States"],"links":[["village","village"],["Montgomery County","Montgomery County#English"],["Missouri","Missouri#English"],["United States","United States#English"]],"glosses":["A village in Montgomery County, Missouri, United States."],"id":"3c2f7f91-a8a6-4404-808c-3bdd987965b6"},{"categories":["en:Places in Texas, USA","en:Places in the United States","en:Unincorporated communities in Texas, USA"],"links":[["unincorporated community","unincorporated community"],["Knox County","Knox County#English"],["Texas","Texas#English"],["United States","United States#English"]],"glosses":["An unincorporated community in Knox County, Texas, United States."],"id":"ea2f9d1f-2f00-49ad-a3ae-67a6cf70a381"},{"categories":["en:Places in Canada","en:Places in Manitoba, Canada","en:Rural municipalities of Manitoba, Canada"],"links":[["Manitoba","Manitoba#English"],["Canada","Canada#English"]],"glosses":["A rural municipality in southern Manitoba, Canada."],"id":"80aba292-4530-462a-8e01-11f7251b3413"},{"categories":["en:Places in Canada","en:Places in Ontario, Canada","en:Villages in Canada","en:Villages in Ontario, Canada"],"links":[["hamlet","hamlet"],["Norfolk County","Norfolk County#English"],["Ontario","Ontario#English"],["Canada","Canada#English"]],"glosses":["A hamlet in Norfolk County, Ontario, Canada."],"id":"6d61204d-3643-4a28-aaef-ee479acd88b9"}],"related":[{"word":"Rhenish"}],"synonyms":[]},"rhinoplasty":{"id":"34119165-f200-4cb6-986a-2740d3e709b5","word":"rhinoplasty","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"plastic surgery used to improve a person's nose","tags":["feminine"],"word":"rinoplastia"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Dr. Sundine specializes in facelifts, necklifts and browlifting, eyelid surgery, as well as rhinoplasty, which involves both technically exacting skill and a keen eye for aesthetic balance.","ref":"2008 January 15, Orange Coast, page 190:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[92,103]],"id":"b817a4f9-a5f2-4591-9f1f-8b708055e222"},{"text":"Those can be signs of emotional immaturity, said Casas, a plastic surgeon in Chicago, Illinois. About 10 percent of her teenage rhinoplasty patients are boys.","ref":"2010 May 4, Madison Park, “Teen's daintier new nose carries bigger regret”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[128,139]],"id":"903558a1-47ff-4d33-a0c6-392ab88198d4"}],"topics":["medicine","sciences","surgery"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","en:Medicine","en:Surgery"],"links":[["medicine","medicine"],["surgery","surgery"],["plastic surgery","plastic surgery"],["nose","nose"]],"raw_glosses":["(medicine, surgery, uncountable) A type of plastic surgery that is used to improve the function (reconstructive surgery) or appearance (cosmetic surgery) of a person's nose."],"glosses":["A type of plastic surgery that is used to improve the function (reconstructive surgery) or appearance (cosmetic surgery) of a person's nose."],"tags":["uncountable"],"id":"a5e1760e-77c9-4f06-9df1-52a8021b5f99"},{"examples":[{"text":"Gone is the era of the cookie-cutter, ski jump nose. Today’s cosmetic doctors are approaching rhinoplasties with a more artistic, individualized approach, using new surgical and nonsurgical techniques to refine rather than revamp one of the most prominent features of the face.","ref":"2020 December 8, Tatiana Boncompagni, “The New Nose: Is the Bump Back?”, in The New York Times, archived from the original on 12 Aug 2020:","type":"quotation","bol